Hi Dr. Yu,

  I am currently trying to load an ASTRAL tree into R, and I've tried both read.tree and read.astral and I have the same error. Because ASTRAL cannot estimate terminal branch length, so some of the edge.length values will be NaN and the trees will be drawn as a cladogram with the following warning:

Warning message:
In fortify.phylo(data, ...) : 'edge.length' contains NA values...
## setting 'edge.length' to NULL automatically when plotting the tree...

Is there a way of getting around this issue?  It seems like you can add dummy values in ASTRAL but I am not sure how (https://github.com/smirarab/ASTRAL/issues/10)

Thanks,

Miles

